A Vehicle Number Plate Recognition (VNPR/ANPR) system is a popular MATLAB project that uses image processing and OCR (Optical Character Recognition). A complete project usually consists of 800–2000+ lines spread across multiple files and uses the Image Processing Toolbox and Computer Vision Toolbox.

Below is a simplified MATLAB program that reads a vehicle image, detects the number plate region, performs OCR, and displays the recognized text.

clc;
clear;
close all;

%% Vehicle Number Plate Recognition System

% Read input image
img = imread('car.jpg');

figure;
imshow(img);
title('Original Image');

%% Convert to Gray Scale
gray = rgb2gray(img);

%% Improve Contrast
gray = adapthisteq(gray);

%% Detect Edges
edges = edge(gray,'Canny');

figure;
imshow(edges);
title('Edge Detection');

%% Morphological Operations
se = strel('rectangle',[5 15]);

dilated = imdilate(edges,se);

filled = imfill(dilated,'holes');

clean = bwareaopen(filled,500);

figure;
imshow(clean);
title('Candidate Regions');

%% Find Connected Components

stats = regionprops(clean,'BoundingBox','Area');

maxArea = 0;
plateBox = [];

for i = 1:length(stats)

    box = stats(i).BoundingBox;
    area = stats(i).Area;

    ratio = box(3)/box(4);

    if area > maxArea && ratio > 2 && ratio < 6

        maxArea = area;
        plateBox = box;

    end

end

%% Crop Number Plate

if isempty(plateBox)

    disp('Number Plate Not Found');
    return;

end

plate = imcrop(img,plateBox);

figure;
imshow(plate);
title('Detected Number Plate');

%% OCR Recognition

result = ocr(plate);

plateNumber = strtrim(result.Text);

disp('=================================');
disp('Vehicle Number Plate');
disp('=================================');
disp(plateNumber);

%% Display Plate on Image

output = insertObjectAnnotation(img,...
    'rectangle',...
    plateBox,...
    plateNumber);

figure;
imshow(output);
title('Recognized Number Plate');
